---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Terms of Service | Fictional History Archive">
  <div class="border-b-2 border-archive-border pb-4 mb-8">
    <h1 class="font-display text-4xl text-archive-paper mb-2">Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="font-sans text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-archive-muted">
      Archivist Access Regulations
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="bg-archive-surface border border-archive-border p-8 space-y-6 text-archive-paper font-serif leading-relaxed">
    <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-widest text-archive-accent font-sans">Effective Date: Implementation of the Archive Protocol</p>

    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl mt-8 mb-4">1. Acceptance of Terms</h2>
    <p>
      By accessing the Fictional History Archive, you acknowledge that you have read, understood, and agree to abide by these multiversal regulations. If you do not agree to these terms, you are directed to immediately disconnect from the mainframe and undergo standard memory wipe procedures.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl mt-8 mb-4">2. Permitted Access and Usage</h2>
    <p>
      The Archive grants you a non-exclusive, non-transferable clearance to view, research, and internally reference the historical documents maintained herein. Unauthorized mass extraction, reality manipulation, or deployment of paradoxical algorithms against the Archive's database is strictly prohibited.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl mt-8 mb-4">3. Submissions and Archival Integrity</h2>
    <p>
      Archivists authorized to submit new records must ensure all data complies with the Archivist's Handbook. The Archive reserves the right to classify, reclassify, or completely redact any submission that violates structural integrity rules or threatens to collapse the internal logic of the catalog.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl mt-8 mb-4">4. Limitation of Liability</h2>
    <p>
      The Archive and its central administration shall not be held liable for any temporal displacement, existential dread, or sudden awareness of alternate selves resulting from the review of our records. Furthermore, we accept no responsibility for actions taken within your local timeline based upon the historical precedents documented here.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl mt-8 mb-4">5. Governing Dimensional Law</h2>
    <p>
      These terms are governed by the overarching principles of multiversal non-interference. Any disputes arising from the use of the Archive will be settled via independent arbitration in a mutually agreeable, neutral pocket dimension.
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
